 a  flamboyant lover of theater and drama  and hole punch is a passionate disco  queen just to name a few  again they are no hooktail or grubba but  at the same time  they are nowhere near as bad and  uninspired as some people made them out  to be  and the way they all have their own  unique traits when it comes to boss  battles like taping the rings together  so you are limited in the way you spin  the arena or how hoe punch takes away  parts of mario's body and decreases his  total hp  makes each one a joy to fight in how  many games are you trying to get your  face back  and i don't mean metaphorically i mean  literally your face is gone  there it is now you have to go get it  back exactly  each battle feels like a puzzle you need  to solve and i  happen to like puzzles even though i'm  bad at them lastly and i think this goes  without saying the music is great as  always  there's so many different tracks in  different styles you can really tell  that the composers had a lot of fun with  this one  all in all i think the game is just a  great little adventure with a lot of  enjoyable moments  the series might not be what it used to  be but that doesn't take away from the  fact that it's obvious that a lot of  love was poured into this game  in fact i think the best way to approach  this game is to just forget that the  thousand year door exists  just take that game set it aside for a  while  and just try to enjoy what is here it's  not a bad game  on the contrary it's a not bad game aka  good  not every game has to be that big  blockbuster or lightning in a bottle  type of game  and just the sheer existence of the  thousand year door is not a valid  argument to hate on origami king it's  meant to be experienced as a standalone  fun little adventure  since this isn't a real review i'm not  gonna rate the game but i would put it  in the same category as luigi's mansion  three  just fun little experiences with some  clever puzzles  simple yet effective stories and some  genuinely funny moments  now if you'll excuse me i have some  whacking to do  [Music]  you
 

